      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(b) The Chief Medical Examiner shall immediately advise the Board of any proposed legislation or proposed administrative directives of other governmental agencies of which he is aware which would affect the operations, powers or duties of the Office of Chief Medical Examiner. Within ten days after an appointment of a medical examiner or of any individual appointed to an important administrative or scientific position the Chief Medical Examiner shall advise the Board of the name and background of any such individual. The Chief Medical Examiner shall advise the Board of any other matter he deems important to the functioning of the Office (but without compromising his independence in performing his duties as Chief Medical Examiner).",
